// A loop "without calls" is not a loop that runs only its own code: a store
// can run a setter or a Proxy trap, a read a getter, an operator the
// valueOf / toString / @@toPrimitive of an operand, a computed key its
// toString, a spread an iterator. Each case walks an Array with
// `for (let i = 0; i < xs.length; i++)` while one such construct in the loop
// body runs code that pops (`_pop`) or pushes (`_push`) the walked Array:
// the loop must see the length change. `a_`: the Array is also held by a
// field of `h`; `s_`: the Array itself carries the code; `w_`: the loop
// stores into the Array. `ctl_` cases run no program code (the loop keeps
// its length: `PERRY_ARRAY_BASE_DIAG=1` prints `[perry quiet] ... verdict=kept`).
// Generated by the setterpop lane's gen.py (PR body); compared with node.
